WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.700
Most earthquakes cluster along plate boundaries, but some occur within plates.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.980
A continental coast is not automatically a plate boundary:

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:12.040
Atlantic passive margins differ from the active western margins of the

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:16.640
Americas. The supplied maps use yellow for 0–70 km, green for

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:21.640
70–300 km, and red for depths greater than 300 km.

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.600
These colors are the source map legend, not the lab’s reading-emphasis

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.600
categories. Mid-ocean ridges have shallow earthquakes.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.480
Subduction zones combine shallow, intermediate, and deep earthquakes along a descending

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:33.880
slab.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.620
Start near the trench and follow the sequence from shallow to

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:41.580
deeper earthquakes. That depth progression traces the inclined slab;

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.960
the deepest dots do not mark the trench.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.120
Near Japan the supplied pattern deepens westward, so the Pacific slab

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:53.000
descends toward the west. Beneath western South America the pattern deepens

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.680
eastward, so the slab descends beneath the continent.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:59.580
A map plots epicenters at the surface and uses color to

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:03.680
encode hypocentral depth. A cross section makes the inclined earthquake zone

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:04.460
easier to see.

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:09.360
The Mediterranean-to-Asia belt includes continental collision and other convergence.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:12.820
Eastern Africa has a diffuse rift-related seismic zone.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:16.500
Low-seismicity interiors separate many active belts.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:19.860
The Aleutians mark subduction south of Alaska;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.720
the San Andreas marks continental transform motion.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:27.040
Hawaii illustrates volcanic and associated seismic activity within a plate.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.240
Shallow seismicity follows the Mid-Atlantic Ridge.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:35.100
Broad ocean interiors and passive margins generally have less seismicity, which

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.940
does not mean zero possible earthquakes.
